After my AWS Free Tier/$100 credits are finished, if I already cancelled the GPay UPI AutoPay, can AWS still charge me?

Short answer: They cannot automatically debit your cancelled GPay AutoPay mandate.

AWS India supports UPI AutoPay for automatic recurring AWS bills. If you cancel the e-mandate, AWS says future bills will need to be paid manually; the automatic payment will no longer work.

However, cancelling AutoPay does NOT make AWS usage free.

If you're on the Paid account plan, after your Free Tier credits are exhausted or expire, AWS charges standard pay-as-you-go rates for billable usage.

===

So:

| Situation                         | What happens                                                      |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Free credits available            | Eligible charges use your credits                                 |
| Credits finished                  | Billable usage can create an AWS bill                             |
| GPay AutoPay cancelled            | ❌ AWS cannot automatically collect that bill through that mandate |
| Outstanding bill                  | ⚠️ You may still owe the amount and need to pay manually          |
| You delete all billable resources | ✅ Future usage charges should stop                                |

===

For your goal — ₹0 payment after Free Tier

Don't rely on cancelling GPay AutoPay. Delete/terminate your billable AWS resources before your credits expire.

For your current project, especially check:

EC2 → Instances → Terminate
EC2 → Elastic IPs → Release unused IP
EC2 → Volumes → Delete unused volumes
SageMaker → Endpoints → Delete any running endpoints
S3 → Buckets → Delete unnecessary resources

AWS specifically recommends shutting down or deleting resources you don't need before Free Tier eligibility expires.

One important distinction

If you are on the new AWS Free account plan, AWS says the account closes automatically when the six-month plan ends or your credits are fully used, and you don't incur charges under that Free account plan.

If you show me your Billing → Free Tier / Credits page, I can tell you whether you are on the Free account plan or Paid account plan and exactly what you need to do to avoid charges.

