I want to cancel my aws account means what is the procedure?

Yes. If you want to permanently cancel/close your AWS account, you can do it from the AWS Console. Since you've finished your project and want to avoid future usage, this is the appropriate option.

Before closing

Your EC2 project can be lost, so make sure anything you want is already saved in GitHub. AWS says you don't have to manually delete every resource before closing, but you should back up anything you want to keep.

Also remember: closing the account does not erase charges already incurred. AWS can send a final bill after closure for usage before the closure date.

Steps to close your AWS account
Sign in to the AWS Management Console as the root user. You cannot close the account while signed in as an IAM user or role.
In the top-right corner, click your account name/account number.
Select Account.
On the Account page, scroll down to find Close account.
Read the closure information.
Enter your AWS account ID when AWS asks you to confirm.
Click Close account.

AWS says you should receive a confirmation email within a few minutes.

Official AWS instructions: Close your AWS account

⚠️ Very important

After closing, AWS keeps the account in a post-closure period for 90 days. You can request reopening during that period, but you remain responsible for any outstanding bills. After that period, the account is permanently closed.

If your main goal is “I want to make sure I don't accidentally get charged”, closing the account is stronger than simply stopping your EC2 instance.

